            {
                "comment": "You're only graded by a few exams, but Matt makes this course sooo much more welcoming and accessible. Do NOT fall behind on material and actually take him up on office hours and asking questions. So kind and passionate. ",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": " The subject is a super difficult one but his slides and explanations make things so much easier to understand. Tests cover a lot of info but questions are pretty fair.",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Class requires a lot of studying but Matt presents the material the most clear, concise, digestible way for truly difficult material. He's more than available for help and genuinely just one of the nicest people ever. Take the class if you can!! It's super interesting and Matt is great.",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Genuinely one of the best professors I've had at UW. He's super accessible and is willing to work with you at anytime. For the course there are 3 lectures (including Professor Reynolds) and he is by far the best lecturer. The class has a lot of hard content, but he does a good job in breaking the complex concepts down. ",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "I loved Dr. Reynolds, but 528 is a HARD class. Lectures are very dense and the whole class is graded on just 3 midterms and a final exam. However, Dr. Reynolds holds office hours (and brings candy), and is very good at explaining concepts in a smaller setting. Also very responsive to email and understanding of student situations.",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Professor Reynold's lectures are interesting and straightforward. Definitely recommend going to office hours as he is great about answering questions, reviewing tough concepts, and clearly cares about helping students learn/succeed in the class. ",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Dr. Reynolds was amazing! Genuinely one of my favorite professors I think I have ever had. He made a very difficult subject completely digestible and I am so grateful I crossed paths with this honestly inspirational man. Go to lectures and go to his office hours, you will learn and he is so eager to help",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 5
